From 9e60cec70e589a199cf86771de4844fe556562d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ronny Stiftel <ronny.stiftel@tomcom.de>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:53:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Commit invasion reward mailboxes before publishing grants and
 ACKs

Stage reward and acknowledgement changes in a copy of the confirmed TradeDesk.
Wait for a checked synchronous completion on the existing WorldWriter FIFO so
older async snapshots finish first. Flush/fsync the temporary ledger, commit its
atomic rename and fsync the containing directory and ancestors before publishing
state or queuing a grant. Keep prior memory and the frozen invasion entitlement
on failure, with a bounded one-second retry backoff.

Load authenticated reward mailboxes from trades.pb independently of world.pb.
Refuse present corrupt/empty ledgers and invalid counters instead of resetting
an already observed grant sequence. Ordinary trade snapshots use the same checked
file/directory persistence primitive; protocol and covenant shapes stay unchanged.

Validation: isolated opc Linux ARM64 Docker build; all 10 focused CTest suites
passed. New fixtures inspect disk inside actual grant delivery before Drain,
restart a trades-only mailbox, order old queued snapshots before a durable ACK,
inject four write-boundary faults, retain failed ACK memory, retry failed grants,
and preserve corrupt/empty ledgers. These are process/fault fixtures, not physical
power-cut tests; successful filesystem fsync semantics remain the storage contract.
No deployed service, configuration, data or unrelated container was changed.

